 partner, friend of high-profile rappers, and criminal-justice reform advocate". Business Insider. April 21, 2021. Retrieved July 5, 2022.\n^ "Coronavirus: MLB jersey provider Fanatics creating masks and gowns for medical workers". March 29, 2020.\n^ Castrovince, Anthony (April 23, 2020). "15,000 masks donated to Cleveland Clinic". Major League Baseball. Retrieved July 6, 2022.\n^ "MLB Officially Partners With Nike And Fanatics; Nike To Be Official Uniform And Footwear Provider". Forbes. January 25, 2019. Retrieved July 5, 2022.\n^ Lee, Michael (April 20, 2020). "Brotherly Love: How a Sixers co-partner is getting stars of all kinds to pitch in". The Athletic. Retrieved July 6, 2022.\n^ Beer, Jeff (May 18, 2020). "How Fanatics\' All In Challenge became the wildest $50 million celebrity charity contest ever". Fast Company. Retrieved July 6, 2022.\n^ Kane, Dr. Gerald C (June 25, 2021). "In Pandemic Pivot, Fanatics Reinvents the Playbook". The Wall Street Journal. Retrieved July 6, 2022.\n^ Young, Jabari (August 13, 2020). "Michael Rubin\'s Fanatics now valued at $6.2 billion after latest Series E funding round". CNBC. Retrieved July 6, 2022.\n^ Herrera, Sebastian (August 13, 2020). "Web Retailer Fanatics Raises $350 Million Amid Rebound in IPO Market". The Wall Street Journal. Retrieved July 6, 2022.\n^ Palmieri, Jean (September 8, 2020). "Fanatics Acquires Assets of Top of the World Headwear Company". Yahoo! Sports. Retrieved July 6, 2022.\n^ Novy-Williams, Eben (September 7, 2020). "Fanatics Expands Headwear Business with Acquisition of Vetta Brands Assets". Sportico. Retrieved July 6, 2022.\n^ Young, Jabari (December 7, 2020). "Fanatics acquires WinCraft, a company that makes sports-themed merchandise". CNBC. Retrieved July 6, 2022.\n^ Young, Jabari (March 24, 2021). "Fanatics valuation doubles to $12.8 billion after a new funding round". CNBC. Retrieved July 6, 2022.\n^ "Fanatics Valuation Rises to $18 Billion as It Plans to Expand Sports Offerings". The Wall Stree