tchell & Ness for $250 Million". Complex Networks.\n^ Golden, Jessica (April 6, 2022). "NFL, MLB and players unions lead the latest round of investment in rapidly growing Fanatics". CNBC.\n^ Gottfried, Miriam (December 6, 2022). "Fanatics Hits $31 Billion Valuation in Latest Funding Round". The Wall Street Journal. Retrieved July 11, 2024.\n^ Gambling Industry News\n^ "US sports giant Fanatics acquires top Italian football club merchandiser". CNBC. April 5, 2023. Retrieved July 11, 2024.\n^ "Fanatics acquires Latin America-based retailer Fexpro". SportsPro. June 14, 2023. Retrieved July 11, 2024.\n^ Golden, Jessica (June 28, 2023). "Fanatics increases its offer to $225 million to acquire PointsBet\'s U.S. assets". CNBC. Retrieved June 30, 2023.\n^ "Q&A: Fanatics Betting CEO Matt King on acquiring PointsBet, innovating a new app and more". USA Today. August 31, 2023. Retrieved July 11, 2024.\n^ "Apax completes acquisition of Bazooka". International Confectionery. October 11, 2023. Retrieved October 19, 2023.\n^ "Andrew Low Ah Kee named new CEO of Fanatics Commerce". FOX Business. September 13, 2023. Retrieved July 24, 2024.\n^ "Nike Lands Major League Baseball Jersey Rights in 10-Year Deal". Bloomberg. January 25, 2019. Retrieved July 24, 2024.\n^ "Fanatics and Lids grow college presence with Barnes & Noble Education investment". SportsPro. December 22, 2020. Retrieved July 24, 2024.\n^ "Inside the deal: PSG and Fanatics\' landmark ecommerce partnership". SportsPro. July 7, 2020. Retrieved July 24, 2024.\n^ "Paris Saint-Germain Signs 10-Year Merchandise Deal With Fanatics". Bloomberg. June 30, 2020. Retrieved July 24, 2024.\n^ "Fanatics lands global e-commerce rights for Olympics merchandise". CNBC.com. October 28, 2021. Retrieved July 24, 2024.\n^ "ESPN: NFLPA, Fanatics Agree to 20-Year Contract for Trading Cards; Joining NBA, MLB". Bleacher Report. Retrieved July 24, 2024.\n^ "With a Frenzy of Deals, Fanatics Swoops In to Reorder the Trading-Card World". The Wall Street Journal. August 19, 2021. Retrieved July 24, 2024.\n^ "Fanatics hires former Dick Clark Productions CEO to lead its collectibles business". CNBC. June 16, 2022. Retrieved July 24, 2024.\n^ Hajducky, Dan (May 22, 2023). "Fanatics buys collectibles auction house PWCC". ESPN.com. ESPN. Retrieved March 26, 2025.\n^ "Fanatics\' Matt King brings new thinking to US sports betting". iGaming Business. May 24, 2023. Retrieved July 24, 2024.\n^ "Fanatics, Connecticut Lottery Open New Retail Sportsbook". Covers. Retrieved July 24, 2024.\n^ "Will Fanatics Upend the World of Sports Collectibles?". The New York Times. January 26, 2024. Retrieved July 24, 2024.\n^ "Fanatics Taps Mannings, Brady, Jeter for Sports-Fan Fest in NYC". Bloomberg. April 11, 2024. Retrieved July 24, 2024.\n^ "WWE & Fanatics Events announce return of WWE World at WrestleMania 41 in Las Vegas". WWE. Retrieved February 5, 2025.\n^\na b c d "Fanatics Fest sets attendance record". Sports Business Journal. June 23, 2025. Retrieved June 23, 2025.\n^\na b Gavin, Mike (June 22, 2025). "Teacher defeats pro athletes in Fanatics competition and makes $250,000 trade with winner Tom Brady". NBC New York. Retrieved June 24, 2025.\n^ https://apnews.com/article/fanatics-studio-tom-brady-olympics-2028-fbe080f9c2c50e13b9cd3530673154d0\n^\na b Kirshner, Alex (March 7, 2024). "It\'s Time for Fanatics to Get Grilled by Congress". Slate. ISSN 1091-2339. Retrieved May 2, 2024.\n^ Auping, Jonny (January 3, 2024). "Fanatics, NFL Sued For Conspiracy To Curb Merch Competition". PPAI Media. Archived from the original on May 2, 2024. Retrieved May 2, 2024.\n^ Leonard, Mike (June 10, 2022). "MLB, Teams, Fanatics Inc. Accused of Online Merchandise Monopoly". Bloomberg Law. Archived from the original on May 2, 2024. Retrieved May 2, 2024.\n^ Arcieri, Katie (November 27, 2023). "Fanatics, Italian Rival Test Antitrust Law in Market Share Fight". Bloomberg Law. Archived from the original on February 15, 2024. Retrieved May 2, 2024.\n^ 