INFO:root:process_current_page returned {'url': 'https://forum.fanatec.com/topic/3762-csl-elite-racing-wheel-officially-licensed-for-ps4%E2%84%A2-csl_e_rw_ps4_eu-does-not-work-on-acc/', 'html': "Jump to content\nSkip to Content\nPRODUCTS\nAPPS\nSUPPORT\nFanatec Holiday Support Update\nHide announcement\nFORUMS\nEVENTS\nNEWS\nLEADERBOARD\nACTIVITY\nExisting user? Sign In\nHome\nFanatec Forum\nRacing Simulations / Racing Games\nAssetto Corsa\nCSL Elite Racing Wheel - officially licensed for PS4™ (CSL_E_RW_PS4_EU) does not work on ACC\nSearch...\nCSL Elite Racing Wheel - officially licensed for PS4™ (CSL_E_RW_PS4_EU) does not work on ACC\nShare\nFollowers\nBenjamin Caspar\nSeptember 23, 2020 in Assetto Corsa\nBenjamin Caspar\nMembers\n4\nposts\n0\nReputation\nSeptember 23, 2020\nHello there,\nmy Setup is:\nCSL Elite Racing Wheel - officially licensed for PS4™ (CSL_E_RW_PS4_EU).\nPC driver 328\nWheel Base Firmware 630\nWheel Base Motor 18\nIssue:\nWhen I start assetto corsa, I have no feedback from my steering wheel (Buttons/Wheel/Pedals). Fanatec steering wheels are suggested to me in the options\nGeneneric Gamepad Configuration Support in Steam is unmarked\nIn F1 2020 i have no problems with my Racing Wheel\nMichael Meßner\nMembers\n26\nposts\n0\nReputation\nSeptember 24, 2020\nOn PC or on Console? On PC you have to load the correct preset shown to you in the options. Hover with the mouse over it and you see a Load-Button.\n\nDriver 328 is very, very, very, very old. 373 or 374 are much better.\nBenjamin Caspar\nMembers\n4\nposts\n0\nReputation\nSeptember 24, 2020\nAUTHOR\n\nOn 9/24/2020 at 1:18 PM, Michael Meßner said:\nOn PC or on Console? On PC you have to load the correct preset shown to you in the options. Hover with the mouse over it and you see a Load-Button.\nDriver 328 is very, very, very, very old. 373 or 374 are much better.\nThanks/Danke Michael,\n\nI use it on PC. I've updated the driver to 373, Base-firmware to 674 and the Motor to 22. But it doesnt changed anything at all.\nI re-installed ACC completely from my PC twice. Now my steering wheel is no longer displayed in the options :( .\nI have this problem since august. An ACC Steam update on 10. September fixed it, but just for one day. Now I have the same problems again.\n\nMichael Meßner\nMembers\n26\nposts\n0\nReputation\nSeptember 24, 2020\nDid you load the preset as I mentioned above? Yoiu have to load it, without loading it it will not work.\nI use ACC since early access and I have the same base.\nBenjamin Caspar\nMembers\n4\nposts\n0\nReputation\nSeptember 24, 2020\nAUTHOR\n[ATTACH=5412]\nYes i did ;-).\nNo matter which button I press, I don't get any feedback in-game.\nBenjamin Caspar\nMembers\n4\nposts\n0\nReputation\nSeptember 24, 2020\nAUTHOR\nUpdate: Now I works... If i change a Keybinding with another key and chance it back the Key will work again....\n3 weeks later...\nLeo Remick\nMembers\n1\nposts\n0\nReputation\nOctober 11, 2020\nI'm in the same boat and the present isn't showing in settings. ACC is not recognizing the wheel or pedals. It's the Fanatec CSL Elite F1 bundle with driver 373 on win 10. It works in other games. How did you get it to work?\nPlease sign in to comment\nYou will be able to leave a comment after signing in\nSign In Now\nGo to topic listing\nHome\nFanatec Forum\nRacing Simulations / Racing Games\nAssetto Corsa\nCSL Elite Racing Wheel - officially licensed for PS4™ (CSL_E_RW_PS4_EU) does not work on ACC\nAll Activity\nLight Mode\nDark Mode\nSystem Preference\nPowered by Invision Community\nCOMPANY\nBlog\nForum\nFanatec Explorer\nFanatec Affiliate Program\nAbout Us\nContact Us\nINFORMATION\nBattery Regulations\nFanatec Consumer Guarantee\nShipping & Delivery\nReturn Policy\nPackage Regulations\nTrademark & Copyright\nABOUT US\nFanatec is the leading brand for dedicated sim racing hardware, including force feedback steering wheels, pedals, and complete cockpits for PlayStation, Xbox, and PC-based racing simulators.\n© 2025 Fanat